*Theorem 1.* _lagassfeld1986 Let $X $ be smooth K3 surface, $H $ ample divisor such that all curves in $| H | $ are integral, then for a general smooth curve $C $ in $| H | $, $C $ is Petri general and all smooth curve $C $ in $| H | $ are Brill-Noether general.  _

_Remark 1._

  +  The condition on $| H | $ is satisfied if $P i c(X)= ZZ[H ]$
  +  a curve $C $ Brill-Noether general if and only if $W^(r)_(d)(C)$ has expected dimension for all $d >= 1, r >= 0 $ where expected dimension is $rho(g,d,r)= g -(r + 1)(g - d + r)$.

 note that if $cal(L) $ on $C $ with $h^(0)(cal(L))= r + 1,deg cal(L) = d $, then $rho(C,cal(L))= g - h^(0)dot h^(1)= rho(g,d,r)$. And $  W^(r)_(d)(C)= {[cal(L) ] in P i c(C): deg cal(L) = d, h^(0)>= r + 1 }  $

